4 0 obj
<<
/Creator ( )
/Producer ( )
/Author ()
/Keywords (*LESSONS LEARNED;*ARTILLERY;*ARMY OPERATIONS;CLOSE SUPPORT;COMBAT SURVEILLANCE;RADAR;COMMUNICATION AND RADIO SYSTEMS;FOLDING FINS\(ROCKETS\);MORTAR LOCATOR RADAR;MILITARY INTELLIGENCE;AIRMOBILE OPERATIONS;ENEMY PERSONNEL;AIRCRAFT AMMUNITION;ARMY TRAINING;SOUTH VIETNAM;VIETNAM)
/Subject (This report covers the period 1 November 1969 through 31 January 1970. During this period the Division Artillery supported maneuver forces in 1st Cavalry Division AM Operation Kentucky Cougar. The 1st Cavalry Division Artillery and supporting fire units provide fire support to 1st Cavalry Division AM maneuver forces within the divisions assigned TAOI and take necessary action to enhance the GVN pacification effort, and to improve the effectiveness of all RVNAF elements. The 1st Cavalry Division Artillery AM continues to act as the maneuver headquarters for AO Chief and control the defenses of the 1st Cavalry Division AM base camp at Phuoc Vinh, RVN. This report describes Task Organization Artillery moves Commanders and Principle Staff Aerial Rocket Artillery Mass Fires.)
/Title (Lessons Learned, Headquarters, 1st Cavalry Division Artillery)
/Filename (/pdf/TR/AD0509007.pdf)
>>
